                {
                  "author": {
                    "__typename": "User",
                    "login": "ZihanWang314"
                  },
                  "body": "Of course yes if the grad norm is divided first. Note that when every micro batch comes in, it only contributes to its fraction in the final batch, both for loss and for grad norm, so I'm very sure to implement correct micro-batching, each micro batch should be forward and backward first (with the loss divided before doing backward), then finally do the norm clip.",
                  "createdAt": "2025-03-04T20:38:54Z",
                  "databaseId": 1980194907,
                  "diffHunk": "@@ -394,8 +394,10 @@ def training_step(self, batch: TensorDict):\n         n_micro_batches = len(micro_batches)\n         step_loss = 0\n         for micro_batch in micro_batches:\n-            loss = self._compute_loss_and_backward(batch=micro_batch) / n_micro_batches\n+            loss = self._compute_loss_and_backward(batch=micro_batch, do_backward=False) / n_micro_batches\n+            loss.backward()\n             step_loss += loss.item()\n+            grad_norm = self.fsdp_model.clip_grad_norm_(max_norm=self.config.optim.clip_grad)",
                  "line": 400,
                  "originalLine": 400,
                  "path": "verl/trainer/fsdp_sft_trainer.py",
                  "updatedAt": "2025-03-04T20:38:54Z",
                  "url": "https://github.com/verl-project/verl/pull/436#discussion_r1980194907"
                }
              ],
              "pageInfo": {
                "endCursor": "Y3Vyc29yOnYyOpK0MjAyNS0wMy0wNFQyMDozODo1NFrOdgdgWw==",
                "hasNextPage": false
              },
              "totalCount": 1
            },
            "databaseId": 2658933158,
            "state": "COMMENTED",
            "submittedAt": "2025-03-04T20:38:54Z",
            "url": "https://github.com/verl-project/verl/pull/436#pullrequestreview-2658933158"
          },
          {
